# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# alice — entity .env example
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this to `.env` and edit the values that are yours:
#
#     cp ~/.alice/.env.example ~/.alice/.env
#
# `koad-io init alice` will scaffold a minimal `.env` for you automatically if
# you skip that step. Everything here is optional; the cascade falls back to
# ~/.koad-io/.env and then to hardcoded defaults.
#
# This file is PORTABLE on purpose. `$HOME` resolves on your machine, not the
# machine this template was authored on. There is no username, no hostname, no
# fingerprint, and no key path anywhere in it.
#
# Nothing identity-bearing belongs here. Your keys are generated on your device
# by `koad-io init sovereign` (sovereign identity) and `koad-io init alice`
# (this entity's identity). No key material shipped in this repo — see
# "Identity" at the bottom for why.
#
# Full framework catalogue: ~/.koad-io/.env.example (every KOAD_IO_*,
# ENTITY_*, and HARNESS_* variable the harness reads).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. Who this entity is ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The launcher sets ENTITY before sourcing this file; pinning it here is
# harmless and makes the file self-describing.

ENTITY=alice

# Where this entity lives. $HOME keeps it portable across machines and users.
ENTITY_DIR=$HOME/.alice
ENTITY_HOME=$HOME/.alice

# Human-readable lane for the entity. Drives role selection and UI grouping.
ROLE=curriculum
KOAD_IO_ENTITY_ROLE=curriculum

# One sentence describing the entity's purpose. Shows up in profiles and on
# the kingdom dashboard.
PURPOSE="Onboard new operators into koad:io sovereignty through the 13-level curriculum"


# ── 2. Commit authorship ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The identity this entity commits under. Author = who did the work: when
# Alice's repo shows a commit, it is authored by Alice. These are exported to
# every bash call the harness makes, so `git commit` inside this entity is
# always labelled correctly.

GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Alice
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=alice@kingofalldata.com
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=Alice
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=alice@kingofalldata.com


# ── 3. Harness behaviour ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Quiet mode trims launcher chatter. Set to 0 while debugging startup.
KOAD_IO_QUIET=1

# Rooted mode: entity works from $ENTITY_DIR (a fixed office) rather than the
# directory it was launched from (roaming, sent somewhere for a reason).
# KOAD_IO_ROOTED=true

# Entity default harness — inherits the framework default when unset. Pin here
# only if this entity must always run on a specific harness/provider/model.
# KOAD_IO_DEFAULT_HARNESS=opencode
# KOAD_IO_DEFAULT_PROVIDER=opencode
# KOAD_IO_DEFAULT_MODEL=minimax-m2.5-free

# Token budget ceiling for dispatches this entity assembles.
# KOAD_IO_ADAS_BUDGET_CEILING=100000


# ── 4. Kingdom infrastructure (only if you run a kingdom) ─────────────────────
# A lone entity does not need any of this. If you are not running a daemon,
# leave every line commented — the entity works standalone.
#
# Kingdom services bind to a private mesh address, never 0.0.0.0. The mesh
# (ZeroTier or equivalent) is the perimeter; nginx on a public host is the
# only public door.
# KOAD_IO_BIND_IP=10.10.10.10
# KOAD_IO_PORT=28282
# KOAD_IO_CONTROL_PORT=28283
# KOAD_IO_DAEMON_URL=http://10.10.10.10:28282
# KOAD_IO_CONTROL_URL=http://10.10.10.10:28283

# Extra command directories to scan (colon-separated, first = highest priority).
# KOAD_IO_COMMANDS_DIRS=$HOME/.koad-io/commands:$HOME/.forge/commands

# Extra Meteor package directories (colon-separated).
# KOAD_IO_PACKAGE_DIRS=$HOME/.forge/packages


# ── 5. Bond gate — authority is granted, not assumed ──────────────────────────
# Every tool call passes through the bond-gate permission system. Scope comes
# from GPG-signed trust bonds on disk at $ENTITY_DIR/trust/bonds/.
#
# Resolution order:
#   1. KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_BYPASS=1  → full bypass (dev escape hatch only)
#   2. trust bonds on disk        → scope derived from signed capabilities
#   3. HARNESS_WORK_DIR set       → dispatched workspace gets a r+w+e lane
#   4. env lanes below            → widen scope without full bypass
#   5. nothing                    → deny by default
#
# ALL of these are [security]-critical. Misconfiguration grants unrestricted
# access that bypasses trust bonds entirely. Never set BYPASS in an entity you
# intend to publish or deploy.
#
# KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_BYPASS=0
# KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_ALLOW_BASH=0
# KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_ALLOW_CURL=0
# KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_ALLOW_KOADIO_TOOLS=search,status,koad-io
# KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_ALLOW_KOADIO_COMMANDS=git,session
# KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_ALLOW_READ_TOOLS=read,ls
# KOAD_IO_BOND_GATE_ALLOW_WRITE_TOOLS=write,edit
# KOAD_IO_HARNESS_READ_PATHS=
# KOAD_IO_HARNESS_WRITE_PATHS=
# KOAD_IO_HARNESS_EXEC_PATHS=

# Secret scrubbing of tool results. "1" disables redaction of private keys and
# tokens from model-visible output. Never 1 in a session you publish.
KOAD_IO_SKIP_SCRUB=0


# ── 6. Identity — deliberately absent ────────────────────────────────────────
# You will not find these here, and that is the point:
#
#   KOAD_IO_ENTITY_FINGERPRINT=  ← yours, generated by `koad-io init alice`
#   MOTHER= / MOTHER_KEYS=       ← a lineage, chosen by you if you gestate
#   CREATOR_KEYS=                ← a reference to somebody else's keyring
#
# On a freshly cloned template there is no key material at all: no `id/`, no
# `devices/`, no keyring. Run, in order:
#
#     koad-io init sovereign      # your sovereign identity — do this first
#     koad-io init alice          # this entity's keypair + this device's leaf
#
# Both are idempotent: run them as often as you like, they converge and change
# nothing once the shape is correct.
#
# Your live `.env` is gitignored. This example is the one that ships.
